# promise: #307
# Settings ▸ Advanced "Search only the current space’s tabs" (#307, not in Arc):
# ⌘T searches and lists the open tabs of the window's space only, typed and with nothing typed.
# Home holds home-a and home-b (in front), Work holds work-a; after the window goes to Work the
# bar finds work-a and none of Home's. A page open only in another space comes back as a history
# row, which opens it here. Off (Arc's bar) finds a tab in any space (TabSearchScopeTests). The last
# readout allows open=0: a background copy can close the bar when its window changes space.
budget rss=600 stalls50=10
seed settings.json {"hasSeenImportPrompt": true, "toolbarDefaultMigrated": true, "showToolbar": false, "commandBarCurrentSpaceOnly": true}
